o-man event with the subtle difference that the East German drivers nominally swapped sleds. " [:a {:href "/athletes/87147"} "Wolfgang Hoppe"] ", the two-man champion, switching from East Germany II to East Germany I and vice versa for " [:a {:href "/athletes/89525"} "Bernhard Lehmann"] ".\nEach of the four runs conformed to the same pattern, East Germany I with the fastest time, East Germany in second with Switzerland I always in third. At the end Hoppe’s crew were 0.5 seconds ahead of their sister crew with only Switzerland I within two seconds of the GDR crews."] "\n\n" [:p {} "Further down the field in twenty-first place " [:a {:href "/athletes/85546"} "Carl-Erik Eriksson"] " of Sweden bade farewell to the Olympic Games. Already in his mid-thirties at the time of his Olympic début in 1964, he was 53 and was the oldest bobsleigh competitor for half a century in this his sixth, and final, appearance."] "\n"] [:table {:class "table table-striped"} [:thead {} [:tr {} [:th {} "Pos"] [:th {} "Competitors"] [:th {} "NOC"] [:th {} "Time"] [:th {} "Run #1"] [:th {} "Run #2"] [:th {} "Run #3"] [:th {} "Run #4"] [:th {}] [:th {}] [:th {}]]] [:tbody {} [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "1"] [:td {} "East Germany 1"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GDR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: middle", :src "https://olympedia-flags.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/GDR.png"}] "GDR"]] [:td {} "3:20.22"] [:td {} "49.65 (1)"] [:td {} "50.18 (1)"] [:td {} "50.18 (1)"] [:td {} "50.21 (1)"] [:td {} [:span {:class "Gold"} "Gold"]] [:td {}] [:td {}]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {}] [:td {:colspan "13"} [:a {:href "/athletes/87147"} "Wolfgang Hoppe"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/98918"} "Roland Wetzig"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/97224"} "Dietmar Schauerhammer"] " • " [:a {:href "/athletes/87978"} "Andreas Kirchner"]]] [:tr {:class "", :style ""} [:td {} "2"] [:td {} "East Germany 2"] [:td {} [:a {:href "/countries/GDR"} [:img {:style "padding-right: 2px; vertical-align: